Haakon Studebaker wrote:

> Since it's been a while, I forgot how to make a crysknife. I got my 
> valkyrie drunk while she was wielding a worm tooth and read a scroll of 
> enchant weapon.
> Ended up with a fireproof worm tooth. A strange item and not what I wanted 
> to have in the first place. Next I read a scroll of enchant weapon while my 
> valkyrie was sober and got a crysknife.
> Yet the fireproofing seems to have gone away.
> 
> Now I'm all curious about the crysknife. I drop it and pick it up a few 
> times until it reverted back to a regular worm tooth and saw that it no 
> longer has fireproofing.
> 
> Is this a bug?

No.  If you RTFL on crysknives (i.e. Dune), you see that they are just 
worm tooths that have been "fixed", and will turn back into worm tooths 
if they are moved away from humans without special equipment.  What this 
means in Nethack is that when you drop a crysknife it turns back into a 
worm tooth.

The reason fireproofing gets involved is that the internal 
representations for fireproofing and fixing are identical, so you can 
freely interchange them.  This is why people sometimes wish for "fixed" 
things other than crysknives, and the get fireproofing, even though it 
does not make sense outside of Nethack.

